From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:38:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8781-zinwa-q25: Supply the GPU power
 domains

MFG0 and MFG1 are powered from the VGPU and VSRAM_GPU rails, as on
other MT6366 boards (mt8186-corsola). The MT6789 power controller
requires the supply for both domains.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
index f5a0e904..104c65a2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -1275,6 +1275,14 @@
  * already in ellyq's tree; the node just needs enabling and its supplies. The
  * vgpu / vsram_gpu rails are coupled (see the mt6366 regulators above).
  * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
+&mfg0 {
+	domain-supply = <&mt6366_vgpu_reg>;
+};
+
+&mfg1 {
+	domain-supply = <&mt6366_vsram_gpu_reg>;
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	mali-supply = <&mt6366_vgpu_reg>;
 	sram-supply = <&mt6366_vsram_gpu_reg>;
